Embedded vs. referenced documents  
Here's a question: “If the user places lots of orders, and each order has its own details, should 
we embed order information in the user document?” The answer is, “No, use referenced 
documents.” Referencing means storing related data in separate documents, linked by an 
identifier. It's ideal to use referenced documents when related data is large, updated 
independently, or occasionally read. 
