What is Node.js Runtime 
The Node.js runtime is an execution environment that allows JavaScript to run outside the browser. 
It combines the V8 JavaScript engine (developed by Google for Chrome) with libuv, a cross-
platform library handling asynchronous I/O operations. 
Unlike traditional server environments that spawn new threads per request, Node.js handles thousands 
of concurrent connections efficiently using its event-driven model. 
