Poll phase — where Node.js spends most of its time  
The poll phase retrieves new I/O events from the operating system and executes their callbacks. Its 
behavior: 
● 1. Calculate timeout - How long to block for I/O 
● 2. Process events - Execute callbacks in the poll queue 
● 3. Check for timers - If timers are due, loop back to timers phase 
The poll phase will block and wait for I/O if the queue is empty and no timers are scheduled, process 
all callbacks in the queue before moving on, and yield to the check phase if setImmediate() callbacks 
are pending. 

