Divide & Conquer Approach: 
1. Divide the array into two equal halves using the middle index.  
2. Recursively find the majority element in the left half and the right half.  
3. If both recursive calls return the same element, return it as the majority candidate.  
4. Otherwise, count the frequency of both candidates in the current subarray.

ts are the same, return that element. 
6. Count the occurrences of both candidates in the current subarray. 
7. Return the candidate whose frequency is greater than half of the current subarray size. 
8. If no candidate satisfies the condition, return -1. 
Complexity Analysis:                
 
Time Complexity: O(n log n)  
 
Space Complexity: O(log n) (Recursion Stack) 
