Naïve Appraoch: with O(n) Time complexity (Not D&C just Naïve Approach) 
Procedure: A simple solution to calculate pow(x, n) would multiply x exactly n times. We can do that 
by using a simple for loop.  

import java.util.Scanner;  

public class CalculatePowerIterative  
{  
public static long power(int x, int n) 
 {  
long result = 1;  
for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) 
 {  
result = result * x;  
}  
return result;  
} 
     public static void main(String[] args) 
    { 
        int x = -2; 
        int n = 10; 
         System.out.println("pow(" + x + ", " + n + ") = " + power(x, n)); 
    } 
} 
Divide & Conquer Approach: 
1. If the exponent n is 0, return 1 (base case).  
2. Recursively compute power(x, n/2) and store the result in a temporary variable.  
3. If n is even, return temp × temp.  
4. If n is odd and positive, return x × temp × temp.

the recurrence relation is: T(n) = T(n/2) + O(1) 
Time Complexity: O(log n)  
Space Complexity: O(log n) (due to the recursion stack) 

